        "title": "✨Ramadan is a deeply significant month for Muslims worldwide, marked by fasting, prayer, reflection, and community. ✨The name “Ramadan” itself comes from an Arabic root word “ramad,” which relates to intense heat, possibly reflecting the original timing of the observance in the Arabian Peninsula. ✨ It is believed that the month of Ramadan was a holy month to Arabs before Islam. During this month, tribal wars would stop, and people would retreat to meditate. ✨Key Aspects of Ramadan are; Fasting (Sawm): Muslims abstain from food and drink from dawn until sunset. This practice is intended to foster self-discipline, empathy for those less fortunate, and increased spiritual awareness. ✨Prayer and Reflection: Increased focus on prayer, including the special nightly prayers called Taraweeh. Ramadan is a time for deep reflection, seeking forgiveness, and strengthening one’s connection with God. ✨ Community and Charity: Ramadan emphasizes the importance of community, with families and friends often gathering for Iftar (the evening meal that breaks the fast). Charitable giving (Zakat) is also a significant aspect of Ramadan. ✨Lunar Calendar: The Islamic calendar is. Opens in new tab.",
